Subject: Adapt keel 0.22.4 call sites to the bumped client-go, slack-go, and distribution APIs

Origin: DHI-internal (package/main/keel dependency bumps)
Description: go/bump replaces raise k8s.io to 0.35.1 and helm.sh/helm/v3 to 3.20.2 (package/main/keel/*/.keel.inc.yaml), which moves distribution/v3 to the 3.1 line. That line moved the reference package to github.com/distribution/reference, client-go 0.35 gives DefaultWatchErrorHandler a context, and slack-go 0.23 replaces FileUploadParameters with UploadFileParameters. Those three call sites are the only source changes needed for the bumped modules to compile. slack-go 0.23 also rejects an upload whose FileSize is 0 before it sends a request, so the Slack call declares the reply's byte length.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/keel-hq/keel.git bc640168f020ab1dc89842938d1883886242a40b
Adaptation: Hunks are against upstream 0.22.4 util/image/reference.go, internal/k8s/pods.go, and bot/slack/slack.go. The go.mod replace pins are not in this patch; go/bump sets them with replaces. Requires for the bumped modules are resolved by go/bump deps and tidy. bot/slack/dhi_upload_test.go is a new file in this patch: a stub-API regression for the long-reply upload path, including multibyte content. The pipeline runs it with go test after go/hermetic, so a zero-length upload fails the build.
Verify: cmd `dhi def build package/main/keel/debian-13/0.yaml` expect go build ./cmd/keel succeeds, the bot/slack upload regression passes, and both leaves pass the package tests
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI dependency bump; upstream 0.22.4 calls the older APIs)
Drop-When: never: the three call sites follow the module APIs that go/bump pins; upstream 0.22.4 calls the older APIs and the patch stays until the pins move back

diff -ruN orig/bot/slack/slack.go new/bot/slack/slack.go
--- orig/bot/slack/slack.go
+++ new/bot/slack/slack.go
@@ -308,11 +308,12 @@
 	}
 
 	// longer messages are getting uploaded as files
-	f := slack.FileUploadParameters{
-		Filename: "keel response",
